leted":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.5 dev 5\n- Reproducible in 4.4.1 stable\n\n### System information\n\nVoid #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Sun May 11 04:22:51 UTC 2025 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce GTX 970 (nvidia; 570.144) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-7600K CPU @ 3.80GHz (4 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nUsing the depth texture as the albedo on an unshaded object in Forward+ or Compatibility results in the object essentially being invisible:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f639810e-36ad-4e96-bafd-4c28be59c7df)\n\nOnly in Compatibility if you enable glow in the environment, the applied texture becomes very dark:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/79a5c376-0446-4319-ae39-46ca27da6bf3)\n\nFrom testing it seems like the texture is almost exactly 4x darker after enabling glow.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Make project using Compatibility\n- Apply the following shader to an object:\n```glsl\nshader_type spatial;\nrender_mode unshaded;\n\nuniform sampler2D screen_texture : hint_screen_texture;\n\nvoid fragment() {\n\tALBEDO = (texture(screen_texture, SCREEN_UV).rgb);\n\t//ALBEDO *= 4.0;\n}\n```\n- Enable glow\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com